                <pb facs="0567" n="485" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg485"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/1800.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to
                            Chile to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1911-05-16"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 16,
                    1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The Chilean minister to Mexico telegraphs the minister for foreign affairs that
                    it seems likely the revolution will succeed, and requests authority to lend his
                    good offices should an opportunity to mediate offer. The minister for foreign
                    affairs stated that such mediation will not be authorized unless perfectly
                    acceptable to the United States. The Chilean chargé d’affaires, upon my
                    suggestion, has been instructed by telegraph to ascertain the Department’s
                    views.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
